            <div xml:id="d88-a1-a10-a4-a1-a2">

                <pb facs="0215" n="175" sameAs="frus:frus1865p1/pg175"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Seaman’s advance note.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Glasgow</hi>,</placeName><hi
                        rendition="#italic">9th day of January,</hi> 1865.</opener>
                <p>Ten days after the departure of the ship Ajax from the last port or place in the
                    river or Firth of Clyde, in which, from any cause, she may be, before finally
                    leaving for the voyage, for which this note is issued, pay to the order of John
                    Melley the sum of three pounds ten shillings, being an advance of wages,
                    provided the said seaman sails in and continuos on board of the vessel, and has
                    previously, and during that period, been duly earning his wages, in terms of the
                    articles of agreement.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>GEORGE M. ADAM.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Messrs. <hi rendition="#small-caps">P. Henderson</hi> &amp; Co., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">West St., Vincent Place.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
